             * the intent-message text above, which now embeds the company
             * name and number directly (§7.3).
             *
             * `payment[company_name]` / `payment[company_id]` still have to
             * reach the server, so they stay as hidden inputs rather than
             * disappearing outright — twoValidatePaymentForm()'s doSave()
             * reads them by name, and fillCompanyData() / initialize() are
             * unchanged: they already write these two elements' `.value`
             * imperatively by id, and do so regardless of which markup mode
             * is rendered.
             *
             * `data-name` is LOAD-BEARING on both, and its absence was the
             * order-intent regression reported on 2026-08-06: with the control
             * in the address area, picking a company dispatched no intent.
             * `data-name` is the contract company-name-payment.phtml resolves
             * the payment step's company pair by — `[data-name="company_name"]`
             * and `[data-name="company_id"]` — and every path that WRITES that
