             * dispatch), and `updatePaymentFields()` itself, where those paths'
             * `dispatch-order-intent` lives. The tile-mode markup below carries
             * the attribute on its visible field, so tile mode dispatched on
             * every pick and this mode dispatched on none — one missing
             * attribute, not a missing code path.
             *
             * NOT total silence, and the distinction matters for anyone
             * diagnosing it again: the `checkout:payment:method-activate` re-arm
             * in that same file dispatches from the STORED selection alone, so
             * an intent could still fire when the buyer activated the method
             * with a company already captured. A feature that fires once and
             * then never again on any pick reads as working intermittently,
             * which is why this took a live report to find rather than a test.
             *
             * The attribute also restores the `update-company-data` sync, so the
             * tile's own component learns the company the address step captured
             * instead of relying on the storage restore in initialize().
             */
            ?>
            <input type="hidden" id="company_name" name="payment[company_name]" data-name="company_name" />
            <input type="hidden" id="company_id" name="payment[company_id]" data-name="company_id" />
            <?php else: ?>
